From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:46:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] S3-CREDITS: a lighter parade ground, bodies due in 5
 ticks, a cheaper ground scan (GBA; credits 29.8 fps, parade 24.1 -> 29.5)

Exact: the ground pass compares one word of the cell (wall, floor texture, light, floor height) with the last ground
cell's instead of byte loads and three compares (overworld.c ow_cell_key); bodyspr_image's hint slot no longer
collides for Hillvile n and Hellvile 500 + n (cross-stream: portrait.c).

Pixel-changing, GBA only (OWNER_DECISIONS VISUAL TRADE-OFFS APPROVED, "a lighter parade ground"):
- DoomoOverworldView.lite (set by credits.c, read only by the GBA's plat_overworld): each open ground cell is a flat fill
  of its texture's average colour at its light level, equal neighbours in one vid_rect (no tile cache lookups, no block
  copies). ~5 ms a frame, which the sprite governor spends on marchers: 6-8 on screen where the tip showed the lead alone.
- a parade body (bodyspr_lazy(3)) is due in PC_BODY_SPAN = 5 ticks instead of PC_STANDIN = 4 on the GBA: a rank (2 bodies)
  is asked 11 ticks before it walks in, and the shorter deadline made 6 of 11 ticks 8-15 ms heavier (cross-stream: portrait.c;
  the PS1 keeps 4).
speed2_story.txt: floors 29 (credits) and 28 (parade), expect-2x2 on a patch of flat grass (20 mixed blocks, textured
ground 127: fails without the flat ground).
Credits 28.6 -> 29.8 fps; parade 24.1 -> 29.4-29.5 fps (51 -> 4-5 frames of 50 ms). Not a steady 30: the remaining 50 ms frames are
the first frame of a body job. Evidence and the gap: docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S3-CREDITS".

